  By Lemma 51 and Equation (2.3), this says that the right derivative of $16 pi \( cal(E) \( s \) - sqrt(a \( s \) \/ \( 16 pi \)) \)$ is strictly negative. The expression is zero at $s = 0$, whereas the supporting-energy inequality and Theorem 2 make it nonnegative for small positive $s$. This is a contradiction.
