  In the regular coordinates of Equation (4.305), the future horizon is $sans(U) = 0$ with area radius $r = sqrt(2 M_0)$. The generator direction $partial_(sans(V))$ is the kernel of its induced form. Thus pullback to any section leaves precisely $r^2 g_(bb(S)^3)$, regardless of the value of $sans(V)$ along the section. A compact connected spacelike section has an angular projection which is a local diffeomorphism and hence a covering of $bb(S)^3$; compactness gives surjectivity, and simple connectedness of $bb(S)^3$ makes that covering a diffeomorphism. The same induced metric holds at the bifurcation sphere. Taking its volume proves the formula. ◻
